---
import AppleIcon from "./AppleIcon.astro";
---

<section class="close">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="halo">
      <img class="mark rise" src="/assets/icon.png" alt="" width="96" height="96" loading="lazy">
      <span class="aura" aria-hidden="true"><b></b><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
    </div>
    <h2 class="rise">That's it. Go make a reel.</h2>
    <div class="cta rise">
      <a class="btn" href="#" data-download>
        <AppleIcon />
        Download for Mac
      </a>
      <a class="btn ghost" href="https://github.com/Alexfrompixel/reelseasy">View on GitHub</a>
    </div>
    <p class="status rise"><b>Where it stands.</b> This is an early preview. I'm about to start running my own clips through it, so expect rough edges. It runs on Apple Silicon Macs with macOS 13 or later. The one-click download is coming. Until then, developers can build it from the source on GitHub.</p>
  </div>
</section>
